<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Final exam problems on hyperbolic functions
-->
<worksheet xml:id="worksheet-exercises-hyperbolic" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>Exercises for <xref ref="chapter-hyperbolic-functions" text="title"/></title>

<introduction>
<p>
A final exam problem on the hyperbolic identities. If you would like to review this topic first, see <xref ref="chapter-hyperbolic-functions" text="title"/>.
</p>
</introduction>

<exercise xml:id="rw23-9-b">
<title>True or False</title>
<statement correct="yes">
<p>
For any real number <m>x</m>, we have
<m>\cosh^2(x) + \sinh^2(x) = \cosh(2x)</m>.
</p>
</statement>
<feedback>
<p>
First,
<md xml:id="eq-rw23-cosh2x" number="yes">
\cosh(2x) = \frac12\left(e^{2x} + e^{-2x}\right).
</md>
Second,
<md xml:id="eq-rw23-sum" number="yes">
\cosh^2(x) + \sinh^2(x)
= \frac14\left(e^x + e^{-x}\right)^2
+ \frac14\left(e^x - e^{-x}\right)^2
= \frac14\left(2e^{2x} + 2e^{-2x}\right)
= \frac12\left(e^{2x} + e^{-2x}\right).
</md>
Comparing <xref ref="eq-rw23-cosh2x"/> and
<xref ref="eq-rw23-sum"/> gives
<m>\cosh^2(x) + \sinh^2(x) = \cosh(2x)</m>.
</p>
</feedback>
</exercise>

</worksheet>
